# Research project organization

Project root is the Python project root. The latest user goal is defined in 01_IDEA/story.md. Read rule05 before template defaults.

- TMM_Transmission_note.md is the research archive; TMM_Transmission_changelog.md records substantive changes.
- 01_IDEA stores purpose, claims, equations, symbols, case plan, validation, figure plan and evidence.
- data stores complete formal inputs. cache stores reproducible intermediates only.
- result/<case_id> stores real states, models, logs, tables, figures and run_manifest.
- tmm_transmission contains newly implemented numerical modules grouped by network, power_flow, reference, statistics, distributions, outputs and workflow.
- TMM_Transmission.py currently checks materials and records environment; it is not an AC or TMM runner.
- tests contains meaningful physics/control/distribution and reproduction checks; copying the template does not run tests.
- 02_PAPER is paper-facing material; 03_REFERENCE stores sources and the original template snapshot.
- Do not introduce scripts/tools or staged coding trees without a concrete reason.
- Template MATLAB files are reference examples only; do not use them as evidence of new implementation.
- Save original attempted inputs, failed states, costs, hashes, models and actual commands. A cache is not a backup.
- Update purpose, profile, note, claims, figures and changelog together when the research scope changes.
